            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Theodore B. Olson, leegin Creative Leather Products, Inc. challenges the per\u2011se illegality rule for resale\u2011price maintenance."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4f464a808a3fa4b8c53674660786fd34c63f3ab4a12d36254c60fb3c42c63f66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4f464a808a3f-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked whether it is difficult to distinguish vertical from horizontal agreements and whether the manufacturer\u2011dealer agreement might create a horizontal accord among dealers."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4f464a808a3fa4b8c53674660786fd34c63f3ab4a12d36254c60fb3c42c63f66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4f464a808a3f-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens, justice Stevens questioned whether a conspiracy among dealers to fix prices could be justified by additional services and competition from other brands."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4f464a808a3fa4b8c53674660786fd34c63f3ab4a12d36254c60fb3c42c63f66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4f464a808a3f-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens also asked why we can be certain that dealer agreements to provide extra services at higher prices are always harmful to consumers."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4f464a808a3fa4b8c53674660786fd34c63f3ab4a12d36254c60fb3c42c63f66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4f464a808a3f-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether any arrangement that produces a higher price is automatically bad under antitrust policy."
      }
    ],
