              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer noted that after the drug industry eliminated resale\u2011price maintenance, margins fell 40\u202fpercent for drugs and 20\u202fpercent for drug stores, and that eliminating RPM for blue jeans saved American consumers about $200\u202fmillion."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ping amicus brief",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4f464a808a3fa4b8c53674660786fd34c63f3ab4a12d36254c60fb3c42c63f66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4f464a808a3f-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ping amicus brief, an amicus brief (Ping) argued that following the Colgate regime is extremely expensive and inefficient, and that manufacturers find it more efficient to use agreements like Leegin\u2019s rather than terminating dealers for discounting."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Underwood",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4f464a808a3fa4b8c53674660786fd34c63f3ab4a12d36254c60fb3c42c63f66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4f464a808a3f-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Underwood, ms. Underwood\u2019s amicus brief emphasized that the per\u2011se rule against resale\u2011price maintenance has been settled law for a century, distinguishing it from other antitrust rules the Court has overturned."
      }
